00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.500
What is your favorite
brand that you could never

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:51.555
imagine saying, for example,
I would say, "Cereal."

00:11:51.555 --> 00:11:56.555
I think I would say limo or
black car but would I say Uber?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.010
I don't even know,

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.010
that's why I'm actually
gonna go the other way.

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.660
Anthony, I'm gonna send it to you.

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:05.440
What is the brand, I'm
gonna think about mine,

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:06.273
cause I really don't have one.

00:12:06.273 --> 00:12:08.120
I'm trying to think,
Captain Crunch cereal.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:08.953
- [Man] Well there you go.

00:12:08.953 --> 00:12:09.930
What cereal, I was like--

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:11.690
- I would go with Captain Crunch cereal.

00:12:11.690 --> 00:12:13.120
But I will tell you, oh
no, I'm not wearing them.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.300
But I will tell you, as I obviously,

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.390
and I'm forcing myself
subconsciously to buy

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.110
a lot more things on Alexa than I think

00:12:19.110 --> 00:12:21.520
I normally would have 'cause I'm curious.

00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:23.407
But I did something that
I didn't think I would do,

00:12:23.407 --> 00:12:26.862
I bought jeans on Amazon through Alexa,

00:12:26.862 --> 00:12:29.160
and didn't care what brand came.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.430
And, to give you the punch
line, they were Diesel.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.523
I had never bought a pair
of Diesel jeans before.

00:12:33.523 --> 00:12:36.042
If you sat here, if we
did this a year ago,

00:12:36.042 --> 00:12:38.600
I would've not thought
that jeans was a category

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.020
I actually didn't care about.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.040
And that's what got me thinking.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.230
I'm like, huh, I would've
thought this is like privacy.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:46.691
I love what people say
versus what they do.

00:12:46.691 --> 00:12:49.943
I would've said, "Jeans is
a category I care about."

00:12:49.943 --> 00:12:52.540
I actually think about
the jeans that I buy

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.170
versus the bottled water

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:56.410
which I definitely would not care about.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:58.944
But yet, in my actions, I
bought three pairs of jeans

00:12:58.944 --> 00:13:00.860
'cause I just needed 'em.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:02.513
And I went for the convenience.

00:13:02.513 --> 00:13:06.180
So, Anthony, what would
definitely be the brand?

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:08.380
Because you love your
deodorants so much, your cereal.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.220
If it was just one,

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.980
if everything else was just commoditized,

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.080
what would be the one brand

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.387
that would come out of
your mouth as, "Alexa,

00:13:14.387 --> 00:13:16.060
"send me Heineken."

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.237
Not beer.

